## Objective
- Implement PJR-0149: add a per-project dashboard page (`execution/generated/dashboard.md` + `dashboard-timeline-gantt.svg`) that aggregates Schedule progress, Timeline track ordering with date-axis Gantt, register status/priority counts, and routine execution/due status from machine-readable sources. This is an **executor stage** (no result file writing; no `.vitepress/` edits).

## Important Details
- **Permission boundaries**: only `docs/**`, `src/**`, `tests/**` are editable; `.vitepress/` and `docs/ja/projects/**/execution/exec/results/**` are denied. Bash allows only: `git status/diff/log/show*`, `npm run *`, `npm test*`, `npx prettier/markdownlint/ajv*`, `specdojo *`, `cat/ls/grep/sed -n *`. No piped/compound commands.
- **Calendar source (condition 4)**: planned start date = `tml-index.yaml` top-level `planned_start_date`; working-day calendar = `sch-defaults.yaml` `calendar` block, accessed via `buildScheduleIndex(schedulePath).calendar`.
- **Dashboard output location**: `<project>/execution/generated/dashboard.md` + `dashboard-timeline-gantt.svg` (gitignored, regenerated by `docs:generate`).
- **VitePress sidebar auto-add**: `vitepress-sidebar` auto-scans docs tree; `generated/*.md` files appear automatically. A curated menu entry (`PROJECTS_FILE_MENU` in `.vitepress/sidebar-config.ts`) cannot be added in this stage — handoff required.
- **Cursor fix applied**: when a wave's tracks have no `catalog_duration_estimate_days`, cursor carries the previous start forward (was resetting to `undefined`).

